==================================================
COUNTDOWN
=========

Create a beautiful JavaScript countdown component.

The requested campaign duration is approximately **one month**.

Do NOT hard-code a misleading "one month" countdown that resets every time someone loads the website.

Create one clearly defined JavaScript campaign end date variable:

const CAMPAIGN_END_DATE = "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS";

The owner can replace it with the lawyer-approved official closing date.

Display:

DAYS
HOURS
MINUTES
SECONDS

Animate the numbers smoothly.

When the countdown reaches zero:

* stop the timer
* display "ENTRY PERIOD CLOSED"
* disable entry buttons
* prevent checkout
* show the official closing message

Do not automatically restart the countdown.

==================================================
ENTRY PAGE
==========

Create a premium multi-step entry interface.

STEP 1 — Choose entry

Only show these two options:

**$5**
1 Entry

**$25**
5 Entries

Do not add other packages.

Make the selected package visually obvious.

STEP 2 — Participant information

Collect:

* Full legal name
* Email address
* Phone number

Add:

* age/eligibility confirmation
* state selection
* agreement to Official Rules
* privacy acknowledgement

Do not ask for unnecessary sensitive information.

STEP 3 — PAYMENT PLACEHOLDER

The user specifically wants the payment area left ready for later integration.

Create a clearly labeled payment section:

**DEBIT / CREDIT CARD**

But DO NOT build a fake card processor.

Do NOT collect or store:

* full card number
* CVV
* PIN
* bank password
* online banking credentials

Instead create a clearly marked integration container:

<!-- PAYMENT PROVIDER INTEGRATION GOES HERE -->

Use a button such as:

"Continue to Secure Payment"

For now, clicking it can display:

"Payment integration pending legal and payment-provider approval."

The owner will later replace this area with the approved bank/payment provider's hosted checkout or tokenized payment solution.

==================================================
VERY IMPORTANT PAYMENT ARCHITECTURE
===================================

Do NOT write JavaScript that stores card information.

Do NOT put secret API keys in frontend JavaScript.

Do NOT create:

localStorage.setItem("cardNumber"...)

Do NOT create fake card validation.

Do NOT send card details to the website's own backend.

Instead leave a clean integration function:

function initializePaymentCheckout(entryData) {
// PAYMENT PROVIDER INTEGRATION HERE
}

The future provider should receive the transaction through its approved secure checkout/tokenization flow.

