==================================================
LEGAL COMPLIANCE CONTENT
========================

Include a prominent notice:

"IMPORTANT: This promotion is not currently accepting entries. The final entry method, eligibility requirements, payment structure, alternative method of entry, official rules and participating jurisdictions are subject to legal review."

Because the property is in Oregon, specifically include a section:

OREGON LEGAL REVIEW

"Participation from Oregon and any other jurisdiction is subject to applicable federal, state and local law and the final Official Rules."

Do NOT say the promotion is legal in Oregon.

Do NOT say the $5 payment model is approved.

Do NOT claim that a lawyer, government agency or regulator has approved anything.

Include a legal-review checklist for the owner:

* Confirm whether the proposed promotion constitutes a lottery, raffle, sweepstakes or another regulated promotion.
* Confirm whether the sponsor is legally eligible to conduct the promotion.
* Determine whether a free alternative method of entry is required.
* Determine eligible jurisdictions.
* Determine state registration/bonding requirements where applicable.
* Determine advertising/disclosure requirements.
* Determine tax treatment of the property prize.
* Determine title-transfer requirements.
* Determine property insurance requirements.
* Determine closing-cost responsibility.
* Determine winner verification requirements.
* Determine privacy/data-retention requirements.
* Review payment processor/bank requirements.
* Review age and residency restrictions.
* Review official odds disclosure.
* Review all state-specific restrictions.

The website must never imply that this checklist itself constitutes legal advice.

==================================================
FTC / CONSUMER DISCLOSURES
==========================

Create a legal-review section that reminds the owner to address:

* whether purchase/payment is required
* whether a free method of entry is available
* how odds are determined
* material costs/conditions
* prize value
* eligibility
* restrictions

The FTC states that legitimate prize promotions do not require payment to participate or win, and if payment is required for a chance at a prize, the promotion may constitute a lottery. Federal and state laws must therefore be reviewed before launch.

Link the legal-review references to official government sources where appropriate.

Do not copy large portions of government text.

